abstract: >-
  Anaxia, the BLLM engine, with the source, Lean development and checks of the paper of the
  same title. A Python package (command anaxia), a Lean 4 library and the container image
  ghcr.io/creelie/bllm-engine: entropy-law check schedules, a typed crossing network of known
  constructions with a program check and a refuter for every candidate, a shared memory, five
  target agents, construction mode (a goal-directed builder and an exists-forall search with an
  independent gate), layer towers of depth one to three, and a registry of the systems and
  collections the engine draws on. Construction mode rebuilds from its rules the gadgets of the
  2016 counterexample to Steinberg's conjecture; none of the five benchmark problems is solved.
